---
import "../styles/global.css";
import BaseHead from "../components/BaseHead.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
---
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <BaseHead
      title="Contact — gelatincalculator.com"
      description="How to reach gelatincalculator.com by email with corrections to bloom values, conversion errors, or questions about the tool."
      path="/contact/"
    />
  </head>
  <body class="bg-white text-stone-900">
    <nav class="border-b border-stone-200">
      <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-5 py-4 flex items-center justify-between">
        <a href="/" class="font-serif text-xl text-stone-900">gelatincalculator.com</a>
        <div class="flex gap-5 text-sm text-stone-600">
          <a href="/about" class="hover:text-amber-700">About</a>
          <a href="/privacy" class="hover:text-amber-700">Privacy</a>
          <a href="/contact" class="text-amber-700">Contact</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </nav>

    <main class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-5 py-16">
      <h1 class="font-serif text-5xl text-stone-900 mb-8">Contact</h1>

      <div class="text-stone-700 leading-relaxed space-y-5">
        <p>
          gelatincalculator.com is a small, independent reference site for
          home cooks working with gelatin. It identifies the likely bloom
          strength of the gelatin you have on hand and converts recipe
          quantities between grades and between sheets and powder. The site
          is built and maintained by one person, and every bloom value it
          publishes was checked against a manufacturer spec sheet, a
          published cookbook, or several independent references before it
          went in.
        </p>

        <p>
          The best reason to write is a correction. If a bloom value on the
          site looks wrong, if a conversion produces a result that does not
          match what a recipe or supplier says, or if you find a broken link,
          a typo, or a page that will not load, please tell me. Corrections
          to conversion data are the most useful mail I get — please include
          the source you are working from so the value can be verified before
          anything is changed.
        </p>

        <p>
          Other things worth writing about: a brand of gelatin with a
          published bloom strength you would like added to the lookup table,
          a conversion the calculator does not currently handle, or a
          question about how a number on the site was arrived at. General
          questions about using gelatin in a recipe are welcome too, though
          the answer will usually be a pointer to the relevant page rather
          than recipe-specific advice.
        </p>

        <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-stone-900 mt-10 mb-3">Email</h2>
        <p>
          <!--email_off--><a class="text-amber-700 underline underline-offset-4" href="mailto:vetorainfo@gmail.com">
            vetorainfo@gmail.com
          </a><!--/email_off-->
        </p>
        <p class="text-sm text-stone-500">
          There is no contact form and no mailing list. Email is the only
          channel, and nothing you send is added to any list or shared with
          anyone. See the <a class="text-amber-700 underline underline-offset-4" href="/privacy">privacy policy</a> for
          what the site does and does not collect.
        </p>
      </div>
    </main>

    <Footer />
  </body>
</html>
